                    Design: We will integrate the                               
                    OneCycleLR scheduler with an AdamW                          
                    optimizer to dynamically vary the                           
                    learning rate between a low start                           
                    (1e-5) and peak (1e-3) over the 5‐epoch                     
                    run, which often yields better                              
                    convergence and generalization than a                       
                    fixed learning rate. We'll set a small                      
                    weight decay (1e‐4) for regularization                      
                    and step the scheduler after each                           
                    batch. All other aspects—including                          
                    EfficientNet‐B3 backbone, data                              
                    augmentations, TenCrop TTA, and                             
                    evaluation pipeline—remain unchanged.                       
