                    Design: We'll replace the single 80/20                      
                    split with 5‐fold stratified                                
                    cross‐validation, training                                  
                    EfficientNet-B0 for each fold and                           
                    computing per‐fold AUROCs. We train                         
                    each fold for 3 epochs to keep runtime                      
                    reasonable, save each fold model, and                       
                    then average their predictions at                           
                    inference for better generalization.                        
                    The script prints the mean CV AUROC and                     
                    defines a `predict(folder_path)`                            
                    function that loads the 5 saved models                      
                    and returns ensemble malignancy                             
                    probabilities for new images.                               
